What is Retrieval?

Retrieval is the process of finding the most relevant chunks from the vector database based
 on the user's question.

 Think of it like Google Search.

You type:

"FastAPI async"

Google doesn't show the entire internet.

It retrieves the most relevant web pages.

RAG does the same thing.

                       RAG Pipeline

                       User Question

                            ↓

                            Embedding Model

                            ↓

                            Question Vector

                            ↓

                            Retriever

                            ↓

                            FAISS

                            ↓

                            Top Matching Chunks

                            ↓

                            LLM

                            ↓

                            Final Answer


Notice:

The Retriever sits between the embedding model and the LLM.

Its job is:

Find the best chunks.

Top-K Retrieval

This is extremely important.

Suppose FAISS gives these similarity scores:

| Chunk   | Cosine Score |
| ------- | -----------: |
| Chunk 5 |         0.96 |
| Chunk 8 |         0.94 |
| Chunk 2 |         0.92 |
| Chunk 1 |         0.74 |
| Chunk 9 |         0.62 |


Similarity Search vs Hybrid vs Reranking

| Technique         | Purpose                                                                            |
| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Similarity Search | Finds semantically similar chunks using embeddings and cosine similarity.          |
| Hybrid Search     | Combines semantic search with keyword search to improve retrieval.                 |
| Reranking         | Reorders the retrieved chunks so the most relevant ones are sent first to the LLM. |


